  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "It is Chefina's birthday and Chef wants to prepare a cake for her. He has NNN points (X1,Y1),(X2,Y2),…,(XN,YN)(X_1, Y_1), (X_2, Y_2), \\ldots, (X_N, Y_N)(X1​,Y1​),(X2​,Y2​),…,(XN​,YN​) in a 2D plane, and a candle which he wants to place at some point in this plane.\n\nThe cake is made up of a non-negative number of layers. Chef considers the deliciousness of the cake to be equal to the number of layers in the cake. A layer is a simple polygon whose vertices are some of Chef's NNN points. It is not required for each of Chef's points to belong to a layer. Furthermore, the layers must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n\nFor each layer, the candle must lie strictly inside it.\nEach of Chef's NNN points that lies strictly inside some layer must belong to some other layer **or be the candle point**.\nNo two layers may touch or intersect.\nThe layers must be chosen in such a way that the deliciousness of the cake is maximum possible.\nNow, Chef is wondering about how the deliciousness of the cake depends on where he places the candle. You should answer QQQ queries. In each query, you are given a point p=(x,y)p = (x, y)p=(x,y) where Chef wants to place the candle and you have to find the deliciousness of the cake.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤5,0001 \\le N \\le 5,0001≤N≤5,000",
      "1≤Q≤2,0001 \\le Q \\le 2,0001≤Q≤2,000",
      "∣Xi∣,∣Yi∣≤109|X_i|, |Y_i| \\le 10^9∣Xi​∣,∣Yi​∣≤109 for each valid iii",
      "∣x∣,∣y∣≤109|x|, |y| \\le 10^9∣x∣,∣y∣≤109",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5,0005,0005,000",
      "the sum of QQQ over all test cases does not exceed 2,0002,0002,000",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (15 points):** N≤12N \\le 12N≤12",
      "**Subtask #2 (20 points):** for each valid iii, Xi=0X_i = 0Xi​=0 or Yi=0Y_i = 0Yi​=0"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ.\nNNN lines follow. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these lines contains two space-separated integers XiX_iXi​ and YiY_iYi​.\nEach of the following QQQ lines contains two space-separated integers xxx and yyy describing a query.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query, print a single line containing one integer ― the deliciousness of the cake.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n6 2\n0 0\n6 0\n3 4\n2 1\n4 1\n3 3\n6 6\n3 3",
        "output": "0\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1:\n\nIn the first query, p=(6,6)p = (6, 6)p=(6,6). The cake cannot have any layers, so its deliciousness is 000.\nIn the second query, p=(3,3)p = (3, 3)p=(3,3). The cake can have only one layer, e.g. a triangle with vertices (2,1),(4,1),(3,4)(2, 1), (4, 1), (3, 4)(2,1),(4,1),(3,4). Other choices of this layer are also possible, but the cake can never have more than one layer."
      }
    ]
